<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador posts $106 mln trade surplus in Oct.</title>
<headline>Ecuador posts $106 mln trade surplus in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador reported a trade surplus of $106 million for October, up from a $12 million surplus in the same month last year, the Central Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Exports reached $414 million, up from the $373 million in October 1995. Imports fell to $308 million from $361 million.</p>
<p>In the ten months of 1996, Ecuador had a trade surplus of $835 million, up from $174 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom 5932 258433</p>
</text>
